# Phase 18 Remoting outbound write-flow parity

Date: 2026-10-24
Branch: phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure
Code commit: 719e5aa3 fix(remoting): match Java outbound write flow
Pinned Java reference: rocketmq-all-5.5.1 at efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9

## Change

Pinned Java 5.5.1 EmbeddedChannel oracle now verifies the outbound write-flow
boundary: sync RPC receives an inbound response before its local outbound
write promise completes; one-way returns before its local write completes and
holds its semaphore until that completion. Rust's connection task now advances
partial outbound writes with a retained offset while continuing to read inbound
frames. Sync/callback/future invoke paths enqueue without applying the operation
deadline to socket progress and immediately wait for response/failure. The
client-owned one-way operation likewise leaves its queued write active after
the call deadline and retains admission through local write completion/failure.

The initial select-loop experiment recreated `write_all` after each inbound
read and failed `p3_inbound_responses_survive_unbounded_outbound_backlog`.
Retaining an offset and using cancellation-safe single writes fixed the byte
replay; the stress regression and full workspace gates passed on final source.

